      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(durable): persist agent turn front doors",
        "body": "## Stack position\n\nPR4 of the durable-core stack, gated on the latest completed ClawSweeper review for PR3 #111278 (overall Gold Shrimp).\n\nThis PR targets `release/2026.7.1`, so GitHub shows the cumulative durable-core stack. The reviewable PR4-only delta is:\n\nhttps://github.com/mjnkao/openclaw/compare/codex/durable-core-pr3-recovery-v5...codex/durable-core-pr4-agent-turn-v1\n\n- Stack parent: `3c344e0a98f34dbb954275f45ca738f744aea3e7`\n- Exact head: `3e3f93666d88b7d3710b92b47ccb2fcf05c41947`\n\n## What changed\n\nPersist durable admission, liveness, and settlement around existing OpenClaw agent-turn and `chat.send` front doors:\n\n- channel reply runner and queued follow-ups\n- CLI Gateway path\n- isolated cron agent execution\n- Gateway `agent` RPC\n- OpenAI-compatible HTTP and OpenResponses streaming\n- `chat.send`\n\nThe implementation reuses the PR2 durable tables and PR3 recovery/owner-attention substrate. It adds no schema, generic executor, parallel worker, or hidden environment-based activation path.\n\n## Contract\n\n- Persist intake before returning a success-shaped acceptance boundary.\n- In `authority` mode, fail closed when intake cannot be persisted.\n- In `observe` mode, remain best effort.\n- In disabled mode, do not open the durable database.\n- Renew a 30-second durable heartbeat while an agent turn is active.\n- Settle success, failure, abort, queue acceptance, and yielded/waiting outcomes through one fenced terminal path.\n- Store message length and SHA-256 hash, not raw prompt text.\n- Mark intake as metadata-only and non-replayable; retry remains an explicit source-owner decision.\n- When a Gateway result becomes uncertain under durable authority, the CLI refuses embedded fallback to avoid duplicate side effects.\n\n## Exact-head live restart proof\n\nAn isolated enabled Gateway reported `OpenClaw 2026.7.1 (3e3f936)`.\n\n1. A normal CLI-to-Gateway turn persisted `agent.turn.received -> running -> succeeded`.\n2. A long tool turn remained `running` through two 30-second heartbeat events.\n3. The Gateway was stopped while the CLI awaited the result.\n4. The CLI exited non-zero with an explicit uncertain-outcome error and did not launch embedded fallback.\n5. On restart against the same SQLite state, startup reconciliation changed exactly one interrupted turn to `lost/lost`, created one open `lost_after_dispatch` fact, and one `restart_interrupted` session wake.\n6. The attached session consumed the durable attention event and ACKed that wake in one attempt.\n7. A separate post-restart CLI turn succeeded normally.\n8. A further restart left the counts unchanged: one lost turn, one uncertainty fact, one ACKed wake, one wake attempt.\n\nThe durable metadata contained only the proof prompt's length and hash; the raw marker was absent.\n\n## Exact-head validation\n\n- durable agent-turn/chat-send/intake tests: 18 passed\n- channel reply/follow-up tests: 143 passed\n- command/CLI fallback tests: 109 passed\n- isolated cron tests: 19 passed\n- Gateway agent/OpenAI/OpenResponses tests: 496 passed\n- chat tests: 560 passed\n- focused chat abort tests: 194 passed\n- `pnpm tsgo:all`\n- changed-file type-aware Oxlint\n- Oxfmt check\n- `git diff --check`\n- exact-head `pnpm build`\n\nAll listed local checks passed at the exact head.\n\n## Boundary\n\nThis PR does not claim arbitrary tool-process resumption, automatic replay from metadata-only intake, exactly-once external side effects, or external-channel delivery. PR5 remains the subagent lifecycle/restart bridge. PR6 remains the read-only operational API/CLI surface.",
        "branch": "codex/durable-core-pr4-agent-turn-v1",
